## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/jp.svg" width="32" alt="Japan" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', position: 'relative', top: '-2px', marginRight: '8px', border: '1px solid #d1d5db', borderRadius: '2px'}} />Japan

Japan has consolidated unprecedented domestic conservative dominance while maintaining international assertiveness under Takaichi's leadership. The LDP's historic 316-seat supermajority—the largest single-party result in postwar history—provides Takaichi with extraordinary governing authority including constitutional amendment capabilities and political capital to pursue assertive positioning on Taiwan contingencies despite Chinese retaliation. Market confidence at record highs (Nikkei 54,782) validates her economic approach while Trump's early congratulations and March summit invitation demonstrate sustained US alliance cooperation. Economic policy continues aggressive fiscal expansion with enhanced electoral mandate, while wage coordination proceeds through spring negotiations. The combination of historic domestic dominance and international assertiveness confirms Japan's transition from reactive alliance management to proactive strategic positioning with maximum political confidence to accept confrontation costs.

**Key developments:**

- **Domestic:** The LDP secured 316 of 465 seats, achieving a two-thirds supermajority and the highest proportion of representatives in postwar Japanese history. Combined with coalition partner JIP, the ruling bloc won 352 seats, significantly expanding from their previous 233-seat majority.
- **Diplomatic:** President Trump congratulated PM Takaichi on her election victory and announced plans to host her at the White House on March 19. Trump had endorsed Takaichi before the election, praising her 'Conservative, Peace Through Strength Agenda.'
- **Economic:** The Nikkei 225 hit an all-time high of 54,782.83, continuing the 'Takaichi trade' that began when she became LDP leader. The market surge reflects investor confidence in her stimulus policies and electoral mandate for economic expansion.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Trump congratulates Takaichi and announces March summit invitation** — US President Donald Trump congratulated PM Takaichi on her election victory and announced plans to host her at the White House on March 19. Trump had earlier endorsed Takaichi before the election, praising her 'Conservative, Peace Through Strength Agenda.' *([reuters.com](https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/trump-congratulates-japans-takaichi-election-win-2026-02-08/))*
- **Takaichi's viral popularity and 'Sana-mania' drives youth engagement** — PM Takaichi's campaign generated unprecedented social media engagement, with her YouTube video surpassing 100 million views. The 'Sana-mania' phenomenon saw young voters embracing everything from her pink pen to handbags, creating a pop culture-like following around Japan's first female prime minister. *([japantimes.co.jp](https://japantimes.co.jp/news/2026/02/05/japan/politics/takaichi-video-message))*
- **Emperor Naruhito hosts Nepal President in Tokyo diplomatic meeting** — Emperor Naruhito and Empress Masako met with Nepalese President Ramchandra Paudel and his wife at the Imperial Palace. The meeting commemorated 70 years of diplomatic relations and included discussion of water advocacy and earthquake assistance. *([ntv.co.jp](https://www.ntv.co.jp/englishnews/articles/2021nkz2b9b5hfpwceub.html))*
- **Toyota names CFO Kenta Kon as new CEO amid profit decline** — Toyota Motor announced CFO Kenta Kon will replace Koji Sato as CEO after the company reported a 43% drop in quarterly profit. Sato will become vice chairman and focus on industry leadership roles including at JAMA and Keidanren. *([insideevs.com](https://insideevs.com/news/786580/toyota-new-ceo-2026/))*
- **Keidanren business lobby invites activist fund Elliott for governance talks** — Japan's most powerful business federation Keidanren invited US activist investor Elliott Investment Management to a closed-door meeting on March 5 to discuss corporate governance issues, highlighting growing shareholder activism in Japan. *([manilatimes.net](https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/02/03/business/foreign-business/japans-top-business-lobby-invites-activist-fund-elliott-for-governance-talks/2269782))*
- **Takaichi meets Nepal President, reaffirms democratic development support** — Prime Minister Takaichi met with Nepalese President Ramchandra Paudel at her office, reaffirming Japan's support for Nepal's democratic development and regional stability. The meeting was part of celebrations marking 70 years of bilateral ties. *([www3.nhk.or.jp](https://www3.nhk.or.jp/nhkworld/en/news/20260204_07/))*
